//****************************************Anotations **************************************
->>.skip() is used to skip the test intensionally.

->>.fixme() in fixme also we are skiping the test but actually the testcase were broken.
in terminal for fixme it shows skipped as it shown in skip anotation the different 
output will get on the html page that the test were broken.

->>.only() this only anotation is used to test only one test case.

->>.step() this anotation is used to group the actions togeather.

->>.slow() it is used to slow the testing triple times than the actual timming.

->>setTimeout(1000) is used to set the time on how much delay we want.

->>.fail() anotation is used to fail the test if really the test were fail then it shows that the testcase were passed but acutally it was failed.

